# Rewritten by compile_port.bat on every successful build (release_date becomes
# today, exe_size the size just linked), so it showed up as a modified file
# after every single compile. Nothing reads it: the auto-updater fetches the
# manifest from the server, and the one that actually gets packaged and
# uploaded is dist\version.json, written separately by package_release.bat.
/app/version.json

# Cores, BIOS and ROMs (NUNCA versionar: violacao de direitos autorais)
/app/cores/
/app/bios/
/app/roms/
/app/games/
/roms/
/games/
/bios/
/cores/
**/bios/
**/cores/
**/roms/
**/games/

# Native PC ports / recomps (Dr. Mario 64, etc.) - downloaded executables and
# assets, the same reasoning as cores/bios/roms above: large third-party
# binaries that do not belong in the repo. port_runner.cpp/.h are the code
# that manages this folder and are tracked normally; only its contents are not.
/app/ports/
/ports/
**/ports/

